{
  "_comment": "The data pack regions. Bounds are minlon,minlat,maxlon,maxlat (WGS84). Basemaps and search packs are cut per region so a phone installs only what it needs; nys (New York plus northern New Jersey) is built whole for older apps (routing-nys.tar, search-nys.sqlite) and New York's search packs are cut from it. core/packs Regions.kt mirrors this file and a unit test keeps the two in step. 'area' (optional) is a polygon of [lon,lat] points: where a point belongs to the region when its box overlaps others; njn's box takes in Staten Island, Rockland and the Bronx, its area is only the New Jersey side of the state line (approximate, within about a kilometre). 'sources' (optional) says which Geofabrik extracts a region is built from: the default is the New York extract cut to the region's own bounds; each entry maps an extract to null (whole), 'self' (cut to this region's bounds) or another region's id (cut to that region's bounds), and several entries are merged (see pipeline/lib/common.sh clip_extract). 'state' (every address in the region is in that state) or 'default_state' (the state of a point in no polygon of 'states'), for the search pack; without either, New Jersey inside njn's area and New York elsewhere (search/states.py). 'osm_only': the search pack is OSM alone, no Overture or NYS Address Points. 'search_from': the bigger search pack a basemap region's own is cut from (New York's regions and njn: search-nys.sqlite, which older apps still download; search/split_search.py). 'all' is the routing build for every state at once, split into routing-main.tar (main roads everywhere) and one routing-<region>.tar of local roads per basemap region (routing/split_tiles.py). 'states' holds the outlines search/states.py needs inside a region that spans several states (Delaware and DC in md). 'planned': built by the pipeline (the states test build) but not shipped or offered yet; the Midwest's twelve regions, one a state, outlines from Natural Earth 10m simplified to about a kilometre (owner, October 2026: 'the entire midwest states, same features as all other states').",
